# 6. Project Objectives

The Adaptive Vehicle Intelligence Architecture (AVIA) project shall pursue the following objectives:

### PO-001 — Establish a Structured Engineering Foundation

Develop and maintain a disciplined systems engineering framework that governs the planning, design, development, validation, and evolution of the AVIA project.

---

### PO-002 — Define a Traceable Engineering Knowledge Base

Establish and maintain a structured engineering repository that preserves project knowledge through governed documentation, version control, engineering reviews, and traceability.

---

### PO-003 — Develop the AVIA System Architecture

Design an adaptive vehicle architecture that integrates multiple engineering disciplines into a coordinated and scalable systems framework.

---

### PO-004 — Support Scientific and Engineering Validation

Apply scientific principles, mathematical analysis, simulation, testing, and engineering evaluation to verify and validate proposed concepts and system designs.

---

### PO-005 — Promote Engineering Innovation

Encourage innovation by identifying engineering constraints, investigating alternative solutions, and developing objective-driven system architectures.

---

### PO-006 — Preserve Engineering Integrity

Ensure that all engineering decisions remain objective, reviewable, traceable, and aligned with the project's engineering philosophy and governance.

---

### PO-007 — Enable Future Expansion

Develop the project in a manner that supports future research, additional engineering domains, new technologies, and continued architectural evolution without compromising engineering consistency.
